    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Obesity drugs are considered at BMI > 27 with comorbidities or 30 without. Orlistat also improves blood glucose and lipids."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Xenical 120 mg PO TID with each main meal containing fat (during or up to 1 h after); higher doses add no benefit. Omit the dose if a meal is missed or has no fat."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "May interact with cyclosporine (give 3 h after orlistat), warfarin, amiodarone, antiepileptics and antiretrovirals."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Flatus, oily stools and diarrhea are common but tend to resolve in the 2nd year; GI effects increase with a high-fat diet (> 30% of calories), so spread fat over three main meals."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
